fd67-293e-41a0-a37a-43f286feaf53"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Payload-shape archaeology (2026-09-06): ADR 0107 is the canonical decision record. It decides `OutboundUpdatePayload` for (outbound, update): at least one of `changed_fields` / `comments` / `labels` / `links` must be non-empty, and `as_legacy_dict()` emits the wrapped shape `{changed_fields, comments, labels, links, local_id}`. This ticket’s description and earthborn-statuelike-boutu point back to that ADR.\n\nCurrent-code evidence favors the wrapped/typed shape for outbound. `outbound_pass.py` constructs `OutboundUpdatePayload(...)` directly; `mutation_payloads.py` validates and serializes the wrapped contract; `single-vast-roan` records the cutover/live DC evidence: outbound_pass constructs typed create/update/delete payloads, `_mutation_to_batch_dict` reads `.fields` / `.changed_fields` unambiguously, and typed-only DC convergence passed. Legacy `differ.py` still has an older flat `payload=changed` outbound/update emitter, so that is the migration surface, not the precedent.\n\nVerdict: resolved-with-evidence. Recommendation for this outbound ticket: migrate the older differ.py outbound/update path to wrapped `changed_fields` / typed `OutboundUpdatePayload`, because ADR 0107 and the newest cutover code already chose that shape.","timestamp":1788763468333352001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD milestone: added RED contract test tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py::test_outbound_update_payload_uses_adr_0107_wrapped_shape; it failed because differ.py emitted flat {'summary': 'new summary'} instead of ADR 0107 wrapped {'changed_fields': {...}, 'comments': [], 'labels': [], 'links': []}. Implemented wrapped payload emission and targeted related tests now pass.","timestamp":1788774252803158001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verification milestone: full make verify passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset using worktree venv after wrapped-payload fix.","timestamp":1788784706111504001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit milestone: change 2782 passed LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, was submitted, and worktree advanced to merged SHA bde9c4e66c7d501221ddc91e38507ed13a4879b2.","timestamp":1788787363841257001}],"created_at":1788109201597861001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"01c0f209-3397-4734-a727-30b776a90807","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a"},{"link_uuid":"141958e2-6329-4f10-b231-b832148baf0a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c3c3-3369-7871-40b8"}],"description":"Discovered while implementing e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a (typed reconciler mutation payload contracts, ADR 0107). ADR 0107 is canonical: outbound/update payloads use OutboundUpdatePayload and its wrapped legacy projection, not the older flat differ.py update payload.\n\nResolved design:\n- Canonical outbound/update payload shape is wrapped: {\"changed_fields\": {...}, \"comments\": [...], \"labels\": [...], \"links\": [...], \"local_id\": ... when present}.\n- outbound_pass.py already constructs OutboundUpdatePayload and is the precedent.\n- differ.py's older _compute_mutations_emit_both path must migrate from payload=changed to the wrapped ADR 0107 OutboundUpdatePayload shape.\n- Do not invent a third shape or compatibility bypass.\n\nWorked example: for an outbound update that changes summary from \"old\" to \"new\", the Mutation payload must contain {\"changed_fields\": {\"summary\": \"new\"}, \"comments\": [], \"labels\": [], \"links\": []}; it must not be {\"summary\": \"new\"}.\n\nSurface parity census:\n- CLI command: out of scope; this is reconciler internals, proven through unit/contract tests rather than a CLI command.\n- MCP/API/library facade: out of scope; no public facade constructs this payload directly.\n- Automated callers: in scope; tests must exercise the differ.py producer used by reconciler automation and compare it to outbound_pass.py/OutboundUpdatePayload serialization.\n- Dual direction: in scope by contrast; inbound/create remains flat per ADR 0107 and must not be changed by this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] differ.py's outbound/update emission uses the ADR 0107 wrapped OutboundUpdatePayload legacy shape with changed_fields/comments/labels/links keys, proven by a contract test that fails against the current flat payload.\n- [x] differ.py and outbound_pass.py/OutboundUpdatePayload agree on the observable outbound/update payload shape for an equivalent field update, including empty comments/labels/links collections.\n- [x] Inbound/create flat payload behavior is unchanged by this outbound/update migration, proven by an existing or new contrast assertion.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- Add or strengthen tests under tests/ to assert the ADR 0107 outbound/update wrapped shape end-to-end for differ.py and the typed OutboundUpdatePayload producer.\n- Run the targeted pytest node(s) covering the new contract and contrast tests.\n- Before pushing, run env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_2 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_2 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py","reason":"Migrate older outbound/update producer to ADR 0107 wrapped OutboundUpdatePayload shape."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"Update stale snapshot-differ documentation to the wrapped outbound/update contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py","reason":"Add RED-first ADR 0107 outbound/update payload contract and inbound/create contrast coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_conflict_resolution.py","reason":"Update differ conflict assertions for wrapped outbound/update changed_fields."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_snapshot_differ_stale_local_state.py","reason":"Update stale snapshot differ precondition to the wrapped outbound/update payload shape."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conflict/test_conflict_resolver_provenance_matrix.py","reason":"Update inline state-advance helper for wrapped outbound/update changed_fields."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","c3c3-3369-7871-40b8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"bd425fce-41dd-4f52-b5ec-44b8b8ceeef2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"162e-57c3-f7d4-4457","ticket_type":"task","title":"Reconcile dual outbound-update payload shapes (differ.py flat vs outbound_pass.py wrapped)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0f712d10-621c-4d32-912d-415b33671353","a01bce17-be26-4746-b72c-f3d442801691","1d9b5e4d-8442-4c8d-979f-7cf8a8ab804e","3b0aa799-0e84-40dd-84c0-9197527698ab","bd425fce-41dd-4f52-b5ec-44b8b8ceeef2","f373f406-ef6d-421b-80f7-71e2059c29f7","cbb4650c-50f3-4301-bc22-45ce17fc0072","04a5fdfe-7bd5-46a5-aa82-efaa35e6d68b","141958e2-6329-4f10-b231-b832148baf0a","7daa7caa-89af-47a2-a53a-de081d4ee867","db6bef7d-5eef-4048-97be-867f103e8d14","fa3dfc1d-3bae-4921-82e7-9edeb2183f19","ca72fd67-293e-41a0-a37a-43f286feaf53"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788788138029364002,"uuid":"953d32b3-2687-4745-b4f2-6f05e69196b8"}